<title>USA: Trimble introduces agricultural system.</title>
<headline>Trimble introduces agricultural system.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trimble Navigation Co Thursday said it introduced its FieldGuide precision agricultural system, designed to improve data capture, field mapping and site-specific application of agricultural chemicals.</p>
<p>The system may be installed in agricultural vehicles, allowing agribusiness, agronomic consultants and producers to use precise Global Positioning System (GPS) data in the field, said Trimble.</p>
<p>The company makes products that use GPS technology for a wide range of applications, including land and hydrographic surveying, mapping, aviation and marine navigation.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (12) 408-8787))</p>
